==Battleground==
*1 [[Oldhorn]] spawns as the boss after 10 seconds<sup>300f</sup>.

==Strategy==
All you need is a way to deal with this one, strong enemy. [[Freshman Cat Jobs (Super Rare Cat)|Cat Jobs]] (any form), [[Sniper the Recruit (Super Rare Cat)|Sniper the Deadeye]] (true form), talented [[Fortune Teller Cat (Rare Cat)|Doctor Cat]], [[Kubiluga (Uber Rare Cat)|Kubilan Pasalan]] (only evolved form), [[Healer (Special Cat)|Healer]] and few other units can completely trivialize this stage, so they should be used if owned. Besides them, there are plenty of cats that can also make a huge difference if used, such as [[Ururun Wolf (Special Cat)|Ururun]], [[Primordial Cat (Rare Cat)|Modern]], [[Onmyoji Cat (Rare Cat)|Thaumaturge]] (do not use if using Cat Jobs), [[Delinquent Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Delinquent Cat]] (true form), talented [[Cat Gunslinger (Rare Cat)|Rodeo]], talented [[Vars (Uber Rare Cat)|Vars]], [[Slime Cat (Rare Cat)|Slime]] and others.

If you use knockback units, bring as many of them as possible alongside some meatshields, also bring knockback up combos and, if using Doctor, some research up combos too. Oldhorn will just be unable to progress and eventually die.

If relying on freeze, slow or weaken, bring many meatshields and as many units with all three of these abilities as you can, while avoiding the less effective options. Wait for Oldhorn to advance a little, then stop him with meatshields, then your units, while saving Healer, if using him, for last. Oldhorn should easily get stuck unable to advance and will quickly fall.

==Trivia==
*This stage has a max enemy limit of 15 despite only having one enemy.
*Oldhorn's description mentions how he's a time travelling prophet that is always too slow to make it back home before the disaster he foresaw, which could be a reference to this stage, and a reason why he is the only enemy you fight here.

